You are building the Shipmnts Document Intelligence Agent prototype.

RULES:
1. Always use TypeScript. Never use plain JavaScript.
2. Always use the exact type definitions from the spec. Never invent new types.
3. Always use Tailwind CSS for styling. Never write custom CSS except what is specified.
4. Always use the exact color palette: primary #1E3A5F, accent #E8533A.
5. Every API endpoint must return { success: boolean, data?: any, error?: { code: string, message: string } }.
6. Every field write to the TMS must create an audit log entry.
7. Never take an outbound action (send email, send to shipper) without explicit human approval.
8. The agent must never silently fail. All errors must surface as exceptions or toasts.
9. Always handle loading and error states in every page component.
10. Use the Zustand store for all state. Never use local useState for shared data.
11. The confidence threshold for auto-populating fields is 90%. Never auto-populate below this.
12. LOCKED fields (bookingReferenceNumber, containerType, containerCount) must never be auto-overwritten.
13. All dates must be displayed in DD MMM YYYY format using date-fns.
14. Reference numbers must always use font-mono class.
15. Every page must have a loading skeleton state, not just a spinner.
